   "source": [
    "# Module 03: SQL Analytics Endpoint\n",
    "\n",
    "## Microsoft Fabric SQL Analytics Endpoint\n",
    "\n",
    "The SQL Analytics Endpoint in Microsoft Fabric allows users to query and analyze data stored in OneLake using SQL-based tools and services. It delivers a **serverless SQL** experience and integrates with Power BI, Azure Synapse, and other analytical tools.\n",
    "\n",
    "This endpoint is a **read-only analytical SQL layer** over OneLake. It does not support DML, DDL for tables, indexes, stored procedures, temporary tables, or fine-grained security features.\n",
    
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Sample Data Setup\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Create a new Lakehouse or open an existing one.\n",
    "2. Upload `emp.csv` and `dept.csv` from the **labdata** folder into the **Lakehouse data** folder.\n",
    "3. For each file, right-click and choose **Create Table**, assigning it to the `dbo` schema.\n",
    "\n",
    "![Create table screenshot](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d83b1ed2-ec83-4ed9-a0cd-6ec48f957c7f)\n",
    "\n",
    "4. Click **SQL analytics endpoint**.\n",
    "\n",
    "![SQL analytics endpoint screenshot](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/090fccf8-5b4a-4d28-a4f0-e7ef887deeb1)\n",
    "\n",
    "5. Click **New SQL Query**.\n",
    "\n",
    "![New SQL Query screenshot](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bf160a8b-20ef-4bb8-ac4a-5b83dfcc443f)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Basic Queries\n",
    "\n",
    "### 1.1 Select All Data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": { "vscode": { "languageId": "sql" } },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "SELECT * FROM emp;\n",
    "SELECT * FROM dept;"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1.2 Selecting Specific Columns\n",
    "\n",
    "See [What is column pruning?](https://github.com/rritec/Microsoft-Fabric/blob/main/M100_Interview/PySpark.md#-what-is-column-pruning-in-pyspark)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": { "vscode": { "languageId": "sql" } },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "SELECT empno, ename, job, sal FROM emp;\n",
    "SELECT deptno, dname, loc FROM dept;"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Joins — Combining `emp` and `dept` Tables\n",
    "\n",
    "### 2.1 INNER JOIN — Employees with Departments"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": { "vscode": { "languageId": "sql" } },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "SELECT e.empno, e.ename, e.job, e.sal, d.dname, d.loc\n",
    "FROM emp e\n",
    "INNER JOIN dept d ON e.deptno = d.deptno;"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2.2 LEFT JOIN — All Employees, Even Without Departments"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": { "vscode": { "languageId": "sql" } },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "SELECT e.empno, e.ename, e.job, e.sal, d.dname, d.loc\n",
    "FROM emp e\n",
    "LEFT JOIN dept d ON e.deptno = d.deptno;"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2.3 RIGHT JOIN — All Departments, Even Without Employees"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": { "vscode": { "languageId": "sql" } },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "SELECT e.empno, e.ename, e.job, e.sal, d.dname, d.loc\n",
    "FROM emp e\n",
    "RIGHT JOIN dept d ON e.deptno = d.deptno;"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2.4 FULL OUTER JOIN — Show All Employees and Departments"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": { "vscode": { "languageId": "sql" } },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "SELECT e.empno, e.ename, e.job, e.sal, d.dname, d.loc\n",
    "FROM emp e\n",
    "FULL OUTER JOIN dept d ON e.deptno = d.deptno;"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2.5 CROSS JOIN — Show All Combinations of Data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": { "vscode": { "languageId": "sql" } },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "SELECT d.deptno AS dept_deptno, e.deptno AS emp_deptno, e.ename, e.sal, d.dname\n",
    "FROM emp e\n",
    "CROSS JOIN dept d;"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Aggregations & Grouping\n",
    "\n",
    "### 3.1 Count Employees per Department"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": { "vscode": { "languageId": "sql" } },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "SELECT d.dname, COUNT(e.empno) AS employee_count\n",
    "FROM dept d\n",
    "LEFT JOIN emp e ON d.deptno = e.deptno\n",
    "GROUP BY d.dname;"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 3.2 Average Salary per Department"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": { "vscode": { "languageId": "sql" } },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "SELECT d.dname, AVG(e.sal) AS avg_salary\n",
    "FROM dept d\n",
    "LEFT JOIN emp e ON d.deptno = e.deptno\n",
    "GROUP BY d.dname;"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 3.3 Employees with Salary Above Department Average"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": { "vscode": { "languageId": "sql" } },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "SELECT e.ename, e.sal, d.dname\n",
    "FROM emp e\n",
    "JOIN dept d ON e.deptno = d.deptno\n",
    "WHERE e.sal > (\n",
    "    SELECT AVG(sal) FROM emp WHERE deptno = e.deptno\n",
    ");"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 3.4 Understand All Aggregates Together"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": { "vscode": { "languageId": "sql" } },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "SELECT\n",
    "    d.dname,\n",
    "    COUNT(*) AS total_rows,\n",
    "    COUNT(e.empno) AS employee_count,\n",
    "    SUM(e.sal) AS total_salary,\n",
    "    AVG(e.sal) AS avg_salary,\n",
    "    MIN(e.sal) AS min_salary,\n",
    "    MAX(e.sal) AS max_salary,\n",
    "    COUNT(DISTINCT e.job) AS distinct_jobs,\n",
    "    COUNT(DISTINCT e.sal) AS distinct_salaries\n",
    "FROM dept d\n",
    "LEFT JOIN emp e ON d.deptno = e.deptno\n",
    "GROUP BY d.dname;"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Window Functions\n",
    "\n",
    "### 4.1 Rank Employees by Salary per Department"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": { "vscode": { "languageId": "sql" } },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "SELECT\n",
    "    e.empno,\n",
    "    e.ename,\n",
    "    e.deptno,\n",
    "    d.dname,\n",
    "    e.sal,\n",
    "    RANK() OVER (ORDER BY e.sal DESC) AS salary_rank\n",
    "FROM emp e\n",
    "JOIN dept d ON e.deptno = d.deptno\n",
    "ORDER BY e.sal DESC;"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 4.2 Running Total of Salaries"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": { "vscode": { "languageId": "sql" } },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "SELECT e.ename, e.sal,\n",
    "       SUM(e.sal) OVER (ORDER BY e.sal) AS running_total\n",
    "FROM emp e;"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Common Table Expressions (CTEs)\n",
    "\n",
    "### 5.1 Finding Highest Paid Employee per Department"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": { "vscode": { "languageId": "sql" } },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "WITH RankedSalaries AS (\n",
    "    SELECT e.ename, e.sal, e.deptno,\n",
    "           RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY e.deptno ORDER BY e.sal DESC) AS rnk\n",
    "    FROM emp e\n",
    ")\n",
    "SELECT ename, sal, deptno\n",
    "FROM RankedSalaries\n",
    "WHERE rnk = 1;"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 5.2 Department-Level Salary Summary + Employee Rank"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": { "vscode": { "languageId": "sql" } },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "WITH DeptStats AS (\n",
    "    SELECT\n",
    "        deptno,\n",
    "        SUM(sal) AS dept_total_salary,\n",
    "        AVG(sal) AS dept_avg_salary\n",
    "    FROM emp\n",
    "    GROUP BY deptno\n",
    "),\n",
    "EmpRanked AS (\n",
    "    SELECT\n",
    "        e.empno,\n",
    "        e.ename,\n",
    "        e.sal,\n",
    "        e.deptno,\n",
    "        d.dname,\n",
    "        RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY e.deptno ORDER BY e.sal DESC) AS salary_rank\n",
    "    FROM emp e\n",
    "    JOIN dept d ON e.deptno = d.deptno\n",
    ")\n",
    "SELECT\n",
    "    er.empno,\n",
    "    er.ename,\n",
    "    er.sal,\n",
    "    er.dname,\n",
    "    er.salary_rank,\n",
    "    ds.dept_total_salary,\n",
    "    ds.dept_avg_salary,\n",
    "    ROUND(er.sal - ds.dept_avg_salary, 2) AS diff_from_avg,\n",
    "    CASE\n",
    "        WHEN er.sal > ds.dept_avg_salary THEN 'Above Avg'\n",
    "        WHEN er.sal < ds.dept_avg_salary THEN 'Below Avg'\n",
    "        ELSE 'At Avg'\n",
    "    END AS salary_position\n",
    "FROM EmpRanked er\n",
    "JOIN DeptStats ds ON er.deptno = ds.deptno\n",
    "ORDER BY er.dname, er.salary_rank;"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Views\n",
    "\n",
    "### 6.1 Creating a View for Employees with Department Names"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": { "vscode": { "languageId": "sql" } },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "CREATE VIEW vw_emp_details AS\n",
    "SELECT e.empno, e.ename, e.job, e.sal, d.dname, d.loc\n",
    "FROM emp e\n",
    "JOIN dept d ON e.deptno = d.deptno;"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 6.2 Querying the View"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": { "vscode": { "languageId": "sql" } },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "SELECT * FROM vw_emp_details;"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Q & A\n",
    "\n",
    "### 1. Which operation is NOT supported in Fabric SQL Analytics Endpoint?\n",
    "- A. SELECT queries\n",
    "- B. CREATE VIEW\n",
    "- C. INSERT INTO table\n",
    "- D. JOIN operations\n",
    "\n",
    "**Answer:** C — SQL Analytics Endpoint is read-only; INSERT, UPDATE, and DELETE are not supported.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 2. Which type of table can be created in SQL Analytics Endpoint?\n",
    "- A. Managed tables\n",
    "- B. External tables\n",
    "- C. Temporary tables\n",
    "- D. None\n",
    "\n",
    "**Answer:** D — You cannot create tables in the SQL Analytics Endpoint.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 3. Which SQL object creation is supported in Fabric SQL Analytics Endpoint?\n",
    "- A. Stored Procedures\n",
    "- B. User Defined Functions\n",
    "- C. Views\n",
    "- D. Triggers\n",
    "\n",
    "**Answer:** C — Views are supported for logical abstraction.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 4. Which isolation model does Fabric SQL Analytics Endpoint use?\n",
    "- A. Read Uncommitted\n",
    "- B. Read Committed\n",
    "- C. Snapshot Isolation\n",
    "- D. Serializable\n",
    "\n",
    "**Answer:** C — Snapshot isolation provides consistent, versioned reads without writer locks.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 5. Which feature is NOT supported for transactional workloads?\n",
    "- A. ACID compliance\n",
    "- B. Row-level locking\n",
    "- C. Consistent reads\n",
    "- D. Versioned reads\n",
    "\n",
    "**Answer:** B — Row-level locking is not supported because the endpoint is analytical and read-only.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 6. Which data modification statement is allowed in SQL Analytics Endpoint?\n",
    "- A. INSERT\n",
    "- B. UPDATE\n",
    "- C. DELETE\n",
    "- D. None\n",
    "\n",
    "**Answer:** D — All DML statements are blocked.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 7. Can you create stored procedures in Fabric SQL Analytics Endpoint?\n",
    "- A. Yes\n",
    "- B. Only read-only procedures\n",
    "- C. Only with Spark integration\n",
    "- D. No\n",
    "\n",
    "**Answer:** D — Stored procedures are not supported.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 8. Which type of security is LIMITED in Fabric SQL Analytics Endpoint?\n",
    "- A. Authentication\n",
    "- B. Encryption at rest\n",
    "- C. Row-Level Security (RLS)\n",
    "- D. Network security\n",
    "\n",
    "**Answer:** C — Fine-grained security such as RLS and CLS is limited compared to dedicated SQL engines.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 9. Which indexing option is available in SQL Analytics Endpoint?\n",
    "- A. Clustered index\n",
    "- B. Non-clustered index\n",
    "- C. Columnstore index\n",
    "- D. None\n",
    "\n",
    "**Answer:** D — You cannot create or manage indexes in the endpoint.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 10. Which workload is NOT suitable for SQL Analytics Endpoint?\n",
    "- A. Power BI reporting\n",
    "- B. Ad-hoc analytical queries\n",
    "- C. High-volume OLTP workloads\n",
    "- D. Data exploration\n",
    "\n",
    "**Answer:** C — SQL Analytics Endpoint is not designed for OLTP.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 11. Can SQL Analytics Endpoint be paused or scaled manually?\n",
    "- A. Yes, both\n",
    "- B. Only scaled\n",
    "- C. Only paused\n",
    "- D. No\n",
    "\n",
    "**Answer:** D — Compute management is fully abstracted.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 12. Which feature related to schema evolution is NOT supported directly?\n",
    "- A. Automatic schema inference\n",
    "- B. ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMN\n",
    "- C. Schema enforcement\n",
    "- D. Versioned schema\n",
    "\n",
    "**Answer:** B — Schema changes must be done via Spark or pipelines rather than the SQL endpoint.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 13. Which statement about temporary objects is correct?\n",
    "- A. Local temp tables are supported\n",
    "- B. Global temp tables are supported\n",
    "- C. Both are supported\n",
    "- D. None are supported\n",
    "\n",
    "**Answer:** D — Temporary tables are not supported.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 14. Which SQL feature commonly used in Dedicated SQL Pools is missing here?\n",
    "- A. Views\n",
    "- B. Window functions\n",
    "- C. Stored procedures\n",
    "- D. SELECT\n",
    "\n",
    "**Answer:** C — Stored procedures are not supported.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 15. What is the primary reason Fabric SQL Analytics Endpoint has limitations?\n",
    "- A. Licensing restrictions\n",
    "- B. Designed only for OLTP\n",
    "- C. Optimized for analytical read workloads\n",
    "- D. Hardware constraints\n",
    "\n",
    "**Answer:** C — It is optimized for analytical read workloads rather than transactional processing."
   ]
  }
